        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "api-contract",
        "title": "Hardcoded sort_keys=False conflicts with user-supplied sort_keys option",
        "explanation": "Serializer options are forwarded to yaml.dump via **self.options. Before this change a caller could pass sort_keys=True (e.g. serializers.serialize('yaml', qs, sort_keys=True)), and it went straight to PyYAML. Now sort_keys=False is also passed explicitly, so supplying sort_keys raises TypeError: dump() got multiple values for keyword argument 'sort_keys'. Separately, sort_keys only exists in PyYAML 5.1+, so older PyYAML versions would raise TypeError on every YAML serialization unless the minimum supported version is at least 5.1.",
        "suggestion": "Use self.options.setdefault(\"sort_keys\", False) next to the allow_unicode default and drop the explicit keyword; make sure the minimum PyYAML requirement is >= 5.1.",
        "evidence": "            sort_keys=False,",
        "confidence": 0.75,
